Third-party data (not covered by the MIT licence above):

1. CFPB Consumer Complaint Database. The structured complaint data is a work
   of the U.S. federal government published by the Consumer Financial
   Protection Bureau for public download. See data/README.md.

2. Consumer complaint narratives. Narratives were published by the CFPB
   under its 2015 Consumer Complaint Narrative Policy (consumer opt-in,
   Bureau scrubbing) until publication ceased on August 14, 2026. Previously
   published narratives are treated by the Bureau as public domain for
   Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) purposes and are proactively disclosed
   in the CFPB FOIA Reading Room; this project uses that archive with a
   pinned snapshot. Narrative text is not redistributed with this
   repository; it is obtained with scripts/download_data.py. Do not use the
   narratives to attempt to re-identify any consumer.

3. SEC EDGAR data (company tickers/CIK mapping and XBRL company facts) is
   published by the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission for public use
   under its fair-access rules. See data/README.md.
